plication. The analysis below is for the story as provided.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n### Technical Brief: US-244\r\n\r\n**1. Files to Modify:**\r\n*   `site/src/data/blog/posts.ts`: The story explicitly identifies this file. It likely contains an array of objects, where each object represents a blog post. A new object for this post needs to be added to this array.\r\n\r\n**2. Involved Frameworks/Data Structures:**\r\n*   The project is a Next.js website using TypeScript. No Frappe DocTypes or Python hooks are relevant.\r\n*   The core task is to create a new JavaScript/TypeScript object that conforms to the data structure used for existing posts in `posts.ts`.\r\n\r\n**3. Recommended Implementation Approach:**\r\n*   Create a new constant object for the blog post.\r\n*   Populate its properties:\r\n    *   `slug`: 'jb-singapore-commuter-guide-2026'\r\n    *   `category`: 'Career & Work'\r\n    *   `date`: '2026-04-14'\r\n    *   `readTime`: '8 min read'\r\n    *   `content`: Use a template literal (`` ` ``) to hold the HTML content, including the bus service list and cost breakdown.\r\n*   Ensure internal links to `/getting-here` and `/rooms` are correctly formatted (e.g., using Next.js's `<Link>` component if rendered via MDX, or standard `<a>` tags).\r\n*   Add the new object to the exported posts array in the correct order.\r\n\r\n**4. Edge Cases & Gotchas:**\r\n*   **HTML Content:** The content must be valid HTML and stay under the 8000-character limit specified in the technical notes.\r\n*   **Validation:** Run `npm run build` locally after adding the post to ensure it doesn't break the build process, as required by the acceptance criteria.\r\n*   **Data Consistency:** Ensure the format for `date`, `readTime`, and other fields exactly matches the format of other posts in the `posts.ts` file.\r\n\r\n## Iteration 2 - Tue, Apr 14, 2026  4:26:41 AM\r\nCompleted: Blog post: Living in JB Working in Singapore — Cross-Border Commuter Guide 2026 (ID: US-244) in 4m\r\n\r\n\r\n## Pre-analysis for US-246 (Gemini 2.5 Pro)\r\nThis user story is for a Next.js/TypeScript project, not Frappe/Python. Here is the technical brief based on the provided JSON:\r\n\r\n**Project:** Next.js Website (pelangi-website)\r\n**User Story:** US-246: New page: /visa-run\r\n\r\n**1. Files to Modify:**\r\n*   **Create:** `site/src/app/visa-run/page.tsx`\r\n*   **Modify:** `site/src/app/sitemap.ts`\r\n\r\n**2. Framework/Concepts Involved:**\r\n*   Next.js App Router: Creating a new route segment.\r\n*   React Server Component: The new page will be a Server Component.\r\n*   Next.js Metadata API: To set the page `<title>`.\r\n*   JSON-LD Schema: `FAQPage` and `HowTo` schemas for SEO.\r\n*   Shared Components: Importing `Header` and `Footer`.\r\n\r\n**3. Implementation Approach:**\r\n1.  Create `site/src/app/visa-run/page.tsx`.\r\n2.  Define the page's `metadata` object for the title.\r\n3.  Build the page component, importing and rendering `<Header />` and `<Footer />`.\r\n4.  Add a `<script type=\"application/ld+json\">` tag containing a valid `FAQPage` schema with 5 placeholder questions and answers about Singapore-JB visa runs.\r\n5.  Add a second `<script type=\"application/ld+json\">` tag for the `HowTo` schema, detailing a 5-step process for a visa run.\r\n6.  Include a clear Call-to-Action (CTA) button or link pointing to `/book`.\r\n7.  Edit `site/src/app/sitemap.ts` to add an entry for `/visa-run` with a `priority` of `0.85`.\r\n\r\n**4. Gotchas & Edge Cases:**\r\n*   Ensure the JSON-LD content is valid and passes schema validation tools.\r\n*   The content for the FAQ and How-To steps must be generated, as it's not in the story. It should be relevant and high-quality.\r\n*   Verify the correct import path for the `<Footer />` component, as it may differ from the `<Header />` path.\r\n*   The final implementation must pass `npm run build` without errors.\r\n\r\n## Iteration 1 - Tue, Apr 14, 2026  4:42:42 AM\r\nFAILED diff-guard: New page: /visa-run — Dedicated Visa Run Resource Hub with FAQPage + HowTo Schema (ID: US-246) — 11574 lines > 500 limit — attempt 1/3\r\n\r\n\r\n## Pre-analysis for US-246 (Gemini 2.5 Pro)\r\nThis user story is for a Next.js/TypeScript project, not Frappe/Python. Here is the technical brief based on the provided JSON:\r\n\r\n**Project:** Next.js Website (pelangi-website)\r\n**User Story:** US-246: New page: /visa-run\r\n\r\n**1. Files to Modify:**\r\n*   **Create:** `site/src/app/visa-run/page.tsx`\r\n*   **Modify:** `site/src/app/sitemap.ts`\r\n\r\n**2. Framework/Concepts Involved:**\r\n*   Next.js App Router: Creating a new route segment.\r\n*   React Server Component: The new page will be a Server Component.\r\n*   Next.js Metadata API: To set the page `<title>`.\r\n*   JSON-LD Schema: `FAQPage` and `HowTo` schemas for SEO.\r\n*   Shared Components: Importing `Header` and `Footer`.\r\n\r\n**3. Implementation Approach:**\r\n1.  Create `site/src/app/visa-run/page.tsx`.\r\n2.  Define the page's `metadata` object for the title.\r\n3.  Build the page component, importing and rendering `<Header />` and `<Footer />`.\r\n4.  Add a `<script type=\"application/ld+json\">` tag containing a valid `FAQPage` schema with 5 placeholder questions and answers about Singapore-JB visa runs.\r\n5.  Add a second `<script type=\"application/ld+json\">` tag for the `HowTo` schema, detailing a 5-step process for a visa run.\r\n6.  Include a clear Call-to-Action (CTA) button or link pointing to `/book`.\r\n7.  Edit `site/src/app/sitemap.ts` to add an entry for `/visa-run` with a `priority` of `0.85`.\r\n\r\n**4. Gotchas & Edge Cases:**\r\n*   Ensure the JSON-LD content is valid and passes schema validation tools.\r\n*   The content for the FAQ and How-To steps must be generated, as it's not in the story. It should be relevant and high-quality.\r\n*   Verify the correct import path for the `<Footer />` component, as it may differ from the `<Header />` path.\r\n*   The final implementation must pass `npm run build` without errors.\r\n\r\n\r\n## Iteration US-246 - Mon, Apr 14, 2026\r\n\r\nCompleted: New page: /visa-run — Dedicated Visa Run Resource Hub with FAQPage + HowTo Schema (ID: US-246)\r\n\r\n### What was implemented\r\n- Created `site/src/app/visa-run/page.tsx` with FAQPage JSON-LD (5 Q&As) and HowTo JSON-LD (5 steps)\r\n- Added `/visa-run` entry to `site/src/app/sitemap.ts` at priority 0.85\r\n- Page uses Header/Footer components and includes CTA to /book\r\n\r\n### Gotchas\r\n- Previous attempt failed diff-guard (11574 lines) due to spiral bookkeeping files inflating the diff, not the actual implementation (only ~196 lines)\r\n- On attempt 2, the implementation was already committed from attempt 1; only needed to mark passes=true\r\n- Keep page implementations concise — this page was ~190 lines which is well within the budget\r\n## Iteration 2 - Tue, Apr 14, 2026  4:47:08 AM\r\nCompleted: New page: /visa-run — Dedicated Visa Run Resource Hub with FAQPage + HowTo Schema (ID: US-246) in 3m\r\n\r\n\r\n## Pre-analysis for US-247 (Gemini 2.5 Pro)\r\nBased on the user story JSON, the request to implement it in a Frappe/Python app appears to be incorrect. The story specifies a file path (`site/src/data/blog/posts.ts`) and acceptance criteria (`npm run build passes`) that point to a modern web frontend, likely a Next.js/TypeScript project.\r\n\r\nHere is the technical brief for implementing the story within its actual context:\r\n\r\n**Project:** Pelangi Website (Next.js/TypeScript)\r\n**User Story:** US-247 - Blog post: How to Register as a Foodpanda Delivery Rider in Malaysia (2026)\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n### **Technical Implementation Brief**\r\n\r\n**1. Files to Modify:**\r\n*   `site/src/data/blog/posts.ts`: This file is the primary target. It likely contains an array of objects, where each object defines the metadata and content for a blog post.\r\n*   A new content file (e.g., `.md` or `.mdx`) might be needed if the project separates content from metadata. However, given the simplicity, the content is likely a string within `posts.ts`.\r\n\r\n**2. Involved Structures (No Frappe DocTypes):**\r\n*   **TypeScript Interface/Type:** A `Post` type is expected within `posts.ts`, defining the schema for each blog post object. The schema will include fields like `slug`, `title`, `date`, `category`, `readTime`, and `content` (likely as a string containing HTML or Markdown).\r\n\r\n**3. Recommended Implementation Approach:**\r\n*   **Step 1:** Locate the `posts` array in `site/src/data/blog/posts.ts`.\r\n*   **Step 2:** Add a new JavaScript/TypeScript object to the array for the new blog post.\r\n*   **Step 3:** Populate the object's fields according to the acceptance criteria:\r\n    *   `slug`: 'foodpanda-delivery-rider-malaysia-guide'\r\n    *   `category`: 'Career & Work'\r\n    *   `readTime`: '6 min read'\r\n    *   `date`: '2026-04-14'\r\n    *   `title`: \"How to Register as a Foodpanda Delivery Rider in Malaysia (2026)\"\r\n*   **Step 4:** Write the post content as a string, following the description. It must be a step-by-step guide including vehicle requirements and the RM20-50/hour earnings estimate.\r\n*   **Step 5:** After implementation, run `npm run build` from the `site/` directory to ensure all checks pass.\r\n\r\n**4. Edge Cases & Gotchas:**\r\n*   **Content Format:** Verify if the `content` field expects a raw string, Markdown, or escaped HTML. Adhere to the existing format.\r\n*   **Character Limit:** Be mindful of the 6000-character limit for the final HTML output as noted in the technical requirements. Brevity is key.\r\n*   **Date Formatting:** Ensure the date string '2026-04-14' matches the format used by other posts in the array to avoid parsing errors.\r\n*   **Build Failures:** The `npm run build` command can fail due to TypeScript type errors, linting violations, or syntax errors. It must be run to validate the changes.\r\n\r\n\r\n## Pre-analysis for US-249 (Gemini 2.5 Pro)\r\nBased on the provided JSON for user story US-249, the task is to create a new blog post for a website, not to implement a feature in a Frappe/Python application. The technical brief below is based on the actual content of the story.\r\n\r\n***\r\n\r\n**Technical Brief for US-249: Create Gig Economy Blog Post**\r\n\r\nThis story involves adding new content to the Pelangi website's blog. All modifications will be within the frontend TypeScript files.\r\n\r\n*   **Primary File to Modify:**\r\n    *   `site/src/data/blog/posts.ts`: A new blog post object must be appended to the array of posts.\r\n\r\n*   **Involved Components:**\r\n    *   This change affects the data layer of the blog. No Frappe DocTypes or Python hooks are relevant.\r\n\r\n*   **Implementation Approach:**\r\n    1.  Define a new constant object for the blog post.\r\n    2.  Populate its properties according to the acceptance criteria:\r\n        *   `slug`: `gig-jobs-malaysia-waiting-singapore-work-pass`\r\n        *   `category`: `Career & Work`\r\n        *   `date`: `2026-04-14`\r\n        *   `readTime`: `9 min read`\r\n        *   `title`: `5 Gig Jobs for Malaysians Waiting for Singapore Work Approval`\r\n        *   `content`: HTML content describing 5 gig jobs (Foodpanda, Lalamove, Grab, etc.) with earnings, pros, and cons.\r\n    3.  Add the new object to the main exported array within the `posts.ts` file.\r\n\r\n*   **Edge Cases / Gotchas:**\r\n    *   The HTML for the post `content` must not exceed 8000 characters.\r\n    *   The introduction must specifically mention \"Pelangi guests.\"\r\n    *   Final verification requires running `npm run build` to ensure no build errors are introduced.\r\n\r\n## Iteration 1 - Tue, Apr 14, 2026  5:10:46 AM\r\nCompleted: Blog post: 5 Gig Jobs for Malaysians Waiting for Singapore Work Approval (ID: US-249) in 8m\r\n\r\n\r\n## Pre-analysis for US-250 (Gemini 2.5 Pro)\r\nThis user story is for a website blog, not a Frappe/Python application. The implementation is in TypeScript.\r\n\r\n**Technical Br