d the new `/singapore-jobs` URL).\n\n**2. Key Framework Elements Involved:**\n*   **Next.js App Router:** The new page will be created at `app/singapore-jobs/page.tsx`.\n*   **React Components:** The page and FAQ accordion will be implemented as functional React components.\n*   **JSON-LD Schema:** A script tag with `type=\"application/ld+json\"` for `FAQPage` must be generated and embedded in the page.\n\n**3. Recommended Implementation Approach:**\n1.  First, create the reusable `FaqAccordion.tsx` component to handle the display of question/answer pairs.\n2.  Next, implement the `generateFAQPage(title, faqItems)` function in `site/src/lib/structured-data.ts`.\n3.  Build the main page component `site/src/app/singapore-jobs/page.tsx`.\n4.  Inside this page, import and use the `FaqAccordion` and call `generateFAQPage` to create the JSON-LD structured data.\n5.  Add the \"Interview Stay Package\" CTA with a pre-filled WhatsApp inquiry link.\n6.  Finally, update `sitemap.ts` to ensure the new page is indexed.\n\n**4. Gotchas and Edge Cases:**\n*   **Diff Size Limit:** The story previously failed due to an `oversized_diff`. Implement changes in small, incremental steps to stay well under the 500-line limit.\n*   **Schema Validation:** The `FAQPage` JSON-LD must be syntactically correct and contain at least 8 question/answer entities to meet acceptance criteria.\n*   **CTA Functionality:** Ensure the WhatsApp link is correctly formatted and URL-encoded to pre-fill the message.\n*   **Build/Lint:** The final code must pass `npm run build` and `npm run lint` without errors.\n\n\n## Iteration 2 - Mon, Apr 14, 2026  5:45:00 AM\nCompleted: Create /singapore-jobs resource hub with FAQPage schema and job seeker CTAs (ID: US-262) — attempt 2\n\n### What was implemented\n- Created /singapore-jobs page with job overview, EP/S Pass/WP comparison table, FAQ accordion, booking CTA with WhatsApp link, and related blog post links\n- Created reusable FaqAccordion component in site/src/components/faq/FaqAccordion.tsx\n- Added FAQPage JSON-LD schema with 8 FAQ items covering work permits, salary, visa sponsorship, and job sectors\n- Updated sitemap.ts with /singapore-jobs URL\n\n### Patterns discovered\n- Visa-run page pattern: inline FAQPage schema as const, no separate structured-data.ts helper needed\n- Existing FAQ.tsx component is hostel-specific; created generic reusable FaqAccordion for topic-specific pages\n\n### Gotchas\n- Previous attempt produced 6609 lines — kept this attempt to 170 lines by using concise FAQ answers and following existing page patterns\n- No structured-data.ts file exists despite technical notes suggesting one; inline schema is the codebase pattern\n## Iteration 2 - Tue, Apr 14, 2026  5:40:05 AM\nCompleted: Create /singapore-jobs resource hub with FAQPage schema and job seeker CTAs (ID: US-262) in 7m","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01Y9cEDpWHT615ZXZPaZ8hSb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good, I now have the story details for US-081. Let me summarize what I need to do:\n\n**US-081: Add Bing Webmaster Tools verification and sitemap submission**\n\n**Acceptance Criteria:**\n1. Bing Webmaster Tools account created at https://www.bing.com/webmasters/ and site verified\n2. Verification via `<meta name='msvalidate.01' content='TOKEN'>` in layout.tsx metadata.verification\n3. Sitemap URL (https://pelangicapsulehostel.com/sitemap.xml) submitted to Bing\n4. Bing crawl report shows pages indexed within 7 days of submission\n5. No crawl errors reported in Bing Webmaster Tools dashboard\n\n**Technical Notes:**\n- Bing Webmaster Tools: https://www.bing.com/webmasters/\n- Next.js metadata verification: `verification: { other: { 'msvalidate.01': 'YOUR_TOKEN' } }`\n- Bing can auto-import verified GSC sites — check for auto-import option first to save time\n- Once verified, submit sitemap via: Sitemaps > Submit Sitemap > enter sitemap URL\n\nThe progress.txt shows this is a Next.js website using TypeScript. I can see from the context that recent work has been on pages like /visa-run, /singapore-jobs, and blog posts.\n\nThis story is about adding Bing Webmaster Tools verification, which is a manual process that requires:\n1. Creating a Bing Webmaster Tools account\n2. Verifying the site via a meta tag\n3. Submitting the sitemap\n4. Monitoring the crawl report\n\nThis is primarily a manual task, but the code part is adding the verification meta tag to layout.tsx.\n\nLet me read the current layout.tsx file to see how metadata verification is configured.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6233,"cache_read_input_tokens":73422,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tok